  "narrative": {
    "intro": "AmerisourceBergen Drug recorded $4.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 298,428 awards with an average award size of $15.8K. Obligations fell 36.6% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $4.7B in the current fiscal year to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs bought $639K and the Department of Justice bought $28K. Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market by obligations at $3.2B, followed by Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $1.5B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $639K. Historical obligations show a rise from $2.1B in FY21 and $2B in FY22 to $4.4B in FY23, $6.1B in FY24, and $7.4B in FY25 before the FY26 to date total of $4.7B. FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial, while the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables report total contract values rather than obligation flows.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who is buying from AmerisourceBergen Drug and in what size?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $4.7B from AmerisourceBergen Drug in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $639K and the Department of Justice obligated $28K. Average award size across all buyers is $15.8K, based on 298,428 awards in the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What products and industries drive AmerisourceBergen Drug federal sales?",
        "body": "Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is the largest market for AmerisourceBergen Drug at $3.2B in obligations. Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers account for $1.5B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing accounts for $639K. These three NAICS categories together represent the bulk of FY2026 to date federal obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
